If you're not on a mount, the lance is basically just another polearm,
useful in several situations, but certainly not an everyday weapon.

Once you have a luckstone and a steed, though, it's a perfectly
serviceable everyday weapon.  It does a little less average damage
than a twoweaponed Excalibur+silver_saber, but it kills the enemy's
movement points, can push enemies back a square, and can hit from two
squares away like a polearm.  The lance can also be twoweaponed, and
Excalibur+lance probably does slightly more damage to non-silver-
hating monsters than Excalibur+silver_saber.  Lance+silver_saber isn't
bad, either, but Knights can only twoweapon at skilled, so you don't
successfully joust as often as if it were your primary weapon only.

If you need to use a shield of reflection for reflection, I think
using an expert lance on a mount is better than Excalibur alone.



